// `abi(.naked)` on a GENERIC function emits a correct naked body.
//
// A generic function is monomorphized through a different Function-creation
// path (lower/generic.zig) than a plain decl. Leaving `is_naked` unset on
// that path ships a FRAMED body for a generic `abi(.naked)` instance — it
// returns 42 but leaks the prologue's stack adjustment (the exact SP-in ≠
// SP-out corruption the `.naked` ABI exists to avoid). generic.zig (and
// the sibling pack-expansion path in pack.zig) set `is_naked` and emit the
// asm-only naked body. This pins that: the monomorphized `answer__i64` is
// a proper naked function (no frame), returning 42. aarch64-pinned (the
// asm body is per-arch); runs end-to-end on a matching host, ir-only
// elsewhere.
answer :: ($T: Type) -> i64 abi(.naked) {
    asm volatile {
        #string A
        mov x0, #42
        ret
A
    };
}

main :: () -> i64 { return answer(i64); }
